-- 0189 — Apple's genre tree, as it answered on 2026-08-15.
--
-- The data half of `0188`. Fifty-six genres, unioned across all 167 storefronts
-- and asked in English, each carrying Apple's own id and the parent Apple
-- states. Generated by `tools/apple_genres.py` and pasted verbatim rather than
-- fetched at migration time: a migration that reaches the network cannot be
-- replayed, and CI has no developer token.
--
-- **The normalised form is Python's**, computed by `normalize_text` before the
-- rows were written here. SQL cannot reproduce that fold, and `0184` is what it
-- costs when the stored form and the computed one differ.
--
-- Twenty-six parent to `hub:music` because Apple files them directly under
-- Music; eleven more because Apple names a parent (`1262` Indian, `1122`
-- Brazilian) that it exposes nowhere; nineteen carry a real parent from the
-- tree — `K-Pop -> Pop`, `Afrobeats -> African`, `Metal -> Rock`.

